{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/947203-balancing-merits","id":947203,"title":"Balancing merits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-09T13:44:57-07:00","id":947203,"title":"Balancing merits","content":"I'd like the communities opinion about this, in three sections.<br /> <br /> 1: For magic items like artifacts, imbued or enhanced items acquired during play. Do people charge merit dots for them? I know if you don't pay for them there is no sanctity of merits on those items but do you engineer the story around loosing said items if they aren't &quot;paid&quot; for with experience?<br /> <br /> 2: For enhanced or imbued items that the mage or cabal could make themselves would you charge merit dots for such items even if you would charge merit dots for items that are scrounged as plunder from an ancient ruin?<br /> <br /> 3: What about other merits that a mage effectively carries around with them? Say a master of Prime who can create his own hallows anywhere he goes or a master of Spirit that can create Loci (essentially the same thing to someone with a familiar). What about a master of Matter or Fate who can pull a gold coin or winning lottery ticket (or penny stock trade) out of his pocket anytime. Would you charge for the Resources merit? <br /> <br /> I know there are spells that effectively give other merits for their duration. Sanctity of merits doesn't apply to them and they are temporary, but they can still be called on whenever needed. <br /> <br /> Just curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous","name":"Servanous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T14:01:10-07:00","id":947210,"title":"","content":"I would consider any imbued or enhanced item and artifacts to be fair game. Sanctity of Merits means the player doesn't lose out as much for having invested in it. I wouldn't charge my players merit dots for items made or found, but I wouldn't make them special targets either unless the story called for it. They could invest merit dots in them if they wanted after finding or making them. Same goes for merits obtained via spells really, they could win the lottery but unless they increase their Resources there will be a reason they run out eventually. Etc.<br /> <br /> In my mind, merits in Mage are pretty fluid since a player can buy them with XP or emulate them with magic, it'd be a pain to try regulating them more than the game does already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T19:25:55-07:00","id":947419,"title":"","content":"Merit dots serve as an abstraction for acquiring those items by means such as Order Status, not crafting them on their own.<br /> <br /> Sure, you can purchase all of that with XP, but all that really does is afford a modicum of plot armor in the instance the ST takes them away. Not that good an investment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}